source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira reads `h1.` at a list item's content start and renders the heading inside the item, so jiro writes the heading as the item's own block rather than keeping the prefix as item text.
-- input.jira --
* h1. y
-- rendered.html --
<ul>
	<li><h1><a name="y"></a>y</h1></li>
</ul>
-- want.md --
- # y
-- warnings.json --
[]
